================================================================================
## Explorer: search results are marked with a visible halo
================================================================================

Context:
After an Explorer search, the entity that matched the search value looked
like every other node. The seed highlight set borderColor / borderSize, but
Sigma's default circle program ignores per-node borders, so only a small size
bump was visible.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   - New _drawSeedHalos(): a DOM layer over the canvases with one pulsing
     ring per highlighted seed.
   - Ring position and size come from getNodeDisplayData,
     framedGraphToViewport and scaleSize, and are redrawn on every
     afterRender, so they follow pan and zoom.
   - Seed nodes are drawn at twice their size; the label is forced and
     boxed (highlighted).
2. src/front/static/query/css/query-sigmagraph.css
   .sg-seed-halo-layer (no pointer events) and .sg-seed-halo (brand-red ring
   with a pulse; static under prefers-reduced-motion).
3. tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py
   New contract tests for the render hook, the positioning inputs and the
   styles.

Checked in headless Chrome with Sigma 3.0.2: the ring stays centred on the
seed after a camera move.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
- src/front/static/query/css/query-sigmagraph.css
- tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py (new)
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-28.log

Test result:
uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/front -> 1783 passed.

================================================================================
## Lakebase registry store: global-config read errors are raised, not hidden
================================================================================

Context:
After yesterday's GlobalConfigService fix the build page still showed the
graph DB under the registry schema, and the branding still fell back to the
default title. The Lakebase compute suspends after 300 s idle. While it woke,
LakebaseRegistryStore.load_global_config caught the read error, logged it at
DEBUG and returned {}. GlobalConfigService therefore saw "no config stored"
instead of a failure, and cached the empty blob for the full TTL; the
failed-read retry and stale-cache paths never ran.
save_global_config merged its updates into that {} too, so a save during
the window could have replaced the stored config.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/GlobalConfig.py
   - load_global_config logs read errors at WARNING and re-raises them.
   - It returns {} only when no row exists for the registry.
   - save_global_config now fails (False, error) when that read fails,
     instead of writing updates merged into {}.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py
   The abstract contract states that read errors raise. Other callers
   (GitHubConfig, GitHubMirror, health probes) already catch exceptions.
3. tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py
   New TestLakebaseGlobalConfigReadErrors: the read error is raised, a save
   whose read fails does not write, and a missing row is {}.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/GlobalConfig.py
- src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py
- tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-28.log

